src/linkage.cpp - hierarchical clustering
------------------------------------------

The nearest-neighbour list algorithm (nn_list_impl(), used for centroid
and median linkage) and the Lance-Williams updates of the distances to a
merged cluster (shared with the nearest-neighbour chain) are a step-by-step
port of hclust.f in R's 'stats'
package (src/library/stats/src/hclust.f):

  F. Murtagh, ESA/ESO/STECF, Garching, February 1986.
  Modifications for R: Ross Ihaka, Dec 1996; Fritz Leisch, Jun 2000;
  Martin Maechler, Apr 2001 and Mar 2014 ("ward.D2").
  Copyright (C) The R Core Team.
  Distributed with R under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or 3.

The nearest-neighbour chain (Murtagh 1983; Mullner 2011) and Prim's
minimum spanning tree (Prim 1957; Gower and Ross 1969) are implemented from
the published algorithms.


src/kmeans.cpp - Hartigan-Wong k-means
---------------------------------------

The Hartigan-Wong algorithm (kmeans_hw_cpp()) is a port of kmns.f in R's
'stats' package (src/library/stats/src/kmns.f), which R's COPYRIGHTS file
describes as based on Applied Statistics algorithms:

  Algorithm AS 136, J. A. Hartigan and M. A. Wong, Applied Statistics
  (1979) 28(1), 100-108.
  Copyright (C) Royal Statistical Society 1979.
  Double precision and declarations for R: B. D. Ripley, 1998;
  M. Maechler, 2001. Copyright (C) The R Core Team.
  Distributed with R under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or 3.


src/dip.cpp - the dip statistic of unimodality
-----------------------------------------------

dip_sorted() follows the C code of the dip in the 'diptest' package
(src/dip.c), with its corrections to the published algorithm:

  Algorithm AS 217, P. M. Hartigan, Applied Statistics (1985) 34(3),
  320-325. Copyright (C) Royal Statistical Society 1985.
  Fortran and S-PLUS code by Dario Ringach; translated to C, corrected
  and extended by Martin Maechler (fixes of 1994 and 2003, the latter
  reported by Yong Lu).
  Copyright (C) Martin Maechler.
  'diptest' is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2
  or later.

The preparation of the values (detection threshold, spreading of ties,
removal of piled-up extremes), the null quantiles of the dip
(data-raw/dip-null.R) and the check of the first principal component are
HeatmapR's own.


Other acknowledgements
----------------------

The default colour scale begins with colours of the viridis colour map by
Stefan van der Walt, Nathaniel J. Smith and Eric Firing, released into the
public domain (CC0).

Dendrogram segments are laid out as in the 'ggdendro' package by Andrie de
Vries and Brian D. Ripley: per merge, the horizontal bar in two halves
meeting at the node, and the two vertical drops.

Colours, transparency, distances, quantiles and medians are computed with
the arithmetic of R's own functions (colorRamp(), rgb(), adjustcolor(),
dist(), cor(), quantile(), median()) so that results match theirs; that
code is written for HeatmapR and is not copied from R.
